   186	## 6. Rank $\le 2$: the explicit finite basis — PROVED
   187	
   188	**Theorem C.** Let $W=I_2(m)$, $m\ge2$ ($m=2$: $A_1\times A_1$; $m=3,4,5,6$: $A_2,B_2,H_2,G_2$), with
   189	order $a<b$ (the other order is symmetric). Put $\langle ab\rangle_k=\Pi_k(a,b)$. The reduced GS
   190	basis of $A(W)$ on $\{\Delta^{-1}<\Delta<a<b\}$ consists of the 8 relations
   191	$$\begin{aligned}
   192	&R_1:\ \langle ab\rangle_m\to\Delta,\quad R_2:\ \langle ba\rangle_m\to\Delta,\\
   193	&R_3^x:\ x\Delta\to\Delta\varphi(x),\quad R_4^x:\ x\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta^{-1}\varphi(x)\quad(x\in\{a,b\}),\\
   194	&R_5:\ \Delta\Delta^{-1}\to1,\quad R_6:\ \Delta^{-1}\Delta\to1,
   195	\end{aligned}$$
   196	$\varphi=\mathrm{id}$ for $m$ even, $\varphi=(a\,b)$ for $m$ odd. The normal forms are
   197	$\Delta^{(k)}w$, $w\in\{a,b\}^*$ without alternating factor of length $m$ (= Garside normal form).
   198	For rank 1 ($A_1$, $N=1$, $\Delta=a$) the reduced basis is $\{a\to\Delta,\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to1,\Delta^{-1}\Delta\to1\}$.
   199	
   200	*Proof (termination and confluence, self-contained).* Validity: $R_1,R_2$ define $\Delta$;
   201	$R_3$ is (G4); $R_4$ follows from $R_3$ ($x\Delta=\Delta\varphi(x)\Rightarrow\Delta^{-1}x=\varphi(x)\Delta^{-1}$,
   202	then replace $x$ by $\varphi(x)$). Each right side is deg-lex smaller (shorter, or same length with
   203	first letter $\Delta^{\pm1}<x$); deg-lex is a monomial well order, so rewriting terminates.
   204	No leading word is a factor of another (positive words of length $m$ vs. length-2 words containing
   205	$\Delta^{\pm1}$), so there are no inclusion compositions. All intersection compositions
   206	(overlaps $w=\bar f c=d\bar g$, $|\bar f|+|\bar g|>|w|$):
   207	
   208	1. $R_i/R_j$, $i,j\in\{1,2\}$: a proper suffix of an alternating word is a prefix of an alternating
   209	   word iff their letters agree, so $w$ is an alternating word of length $m+j$, $1\le j\le m-1$.
   210	   Write $w=w'\,\bar g=\bar f\,w''$ with $|w'|=|w''|=j$. Then $w\to\Delta w''$ and
   211	   $w\to w'\Delta\to^*\Delta\varphi(w')$ by $j$ applications of $R_3$. Positions $i$ and $i+m$ of an
   212	   alternating word carry the same letter iff $m$ is even, so $w''=\varphi(w')$: joinable.
   213	2. $R_{1,2}/R_3$: $w=\bar f\Delta$ with $\bar f=f'x$ alternating of length $m$:
   214	   $w\to\Delta\Delta$; $w\to f'\Delta\varphi(x)\to^*\Delta\varphi(f')\varphi(x)=\Delta\varphi(\bar f)\to\Delta\Delta$
   215	   ($\varphi(\bar f)$ is alternating of length $m$).
   216	3. $R_{1,2}/R_4$: $w=\bar f\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to1$;
   217	   $w\to f'\Delta^{-1}\varphi(x)\to^*\Delta^{-1}\varphi(\bar f)\to\Delta^{-1}\Delta\to1$.
   218	4. $R_3/R_5$: $x\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to x$; $x\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta\varphi(x)\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta\Delta^{-1}x\to x$.
   219	5. $R_4/R_6$: symmetric to 4.
   220	6. $R_5/R_6$, $R_6/R_5$: $\Delta\Delta^{-1}\Delta\to\Delta$ both ways; $\Delta^{-1}\Delta\Delta^{-1}\to\Delta^{-1}$ both ways.
   221	
   222	These are all overlaps: suffixes of leading words that are prefixes of leading words are a letter
   223	$x$ (suffix of $R_{1,2}$; prefixes of $R_{1,2},R_3^x,R_4^x$), $\Delta$ (suffix of $R_3,R_6$; prefix
   224	of $R_5$) and $\Delta^{-1}$ (suffix of $R_4,R_5$; prefix of $R_6$), plus longer alternating
   225	suffixes in case 1. By the Composition–Diamond lemma $S$ is a GS basis; the original relations
   226	are consequences of $S$, and $S$ holds in $A$, so $\langle X|S\rangle=A$. The irreducible words are
   227	$\Delta^{(k)}w$ with $w$ avoiding $\langle ab\rangle_m,\langle ba\rangle_m$, and $\Delta$-letters
   228	first, as stated. Rank 1 is immediate. ∎
   229	
   230	(Machine re-check for $m=3,\dots,12$: `work/certify.py I2_m`, all checks pass;
   231	`evidence/certify/`.)
