   367	**Corollary (classification of bounded bases).** For an irreducible finite Coxeter type $W$ the
   368	following are equivalent: (a) for some order of $S$ the leading words of the reduced deg-lex GS
   369	basis of $A(W)$ on the Artin–Garside alphabet form a finite union of families
   370	$u_0v_1^{*}u_1\cdots v_r^{*}u_r$ ($u_i,v_i$ words); (b) $\operatorname{rank}W\le3$ or $W=D_4$. Then the
   371	basis is finite iff $\operatorname{rank}W\le2$. *Proof.* (b)⇒(a): Theorems C, E, F. (a)⇒(b): such a
   372	union has polynomially bounded counts, while §8 gives exponential growth for every order when
   373	$W\in\{A_n,B_n\ (n\ge4),D_n\ (n\ge5),E_{6,7,8},F_4,H_4\}$. Status: COMPUTED+VERIFIED (relies on the
   374	computer-assisted parts of §§7–8).
