   105	## State of the art
   106	
   107	- **Type $A$, book alphabets:** Artin–Garside (Bokut, JSC 43 (2008) 397–405), Artin–Burau
   108	  (Bokut–Chainikov–Shum, Comm. Algebra 35 (2007)), BKL with $\delta^{\pm1}$ (Bokut, J. Algebra 321 (2009)),
   109	  Adyan–Thurston (Chen–Zhong, Algebra Colloq. 20 (2013)); positive braid monoid (Bokut–Fong–Ke–Shiao 2003).
   110	- **Rank 2:** positive dihedral Artin monoids, infinite deg-lex completion (Autord, arXiv:0712.0525,
   111	  Prop. 3.4); all two-generator Artin groups in HNN/free-by-cyclic generators with a tower order
   112	  (Bokut–Vesnin, JSC 41 (2006)); standard signed generators shortlex automatic (Holt–Rees,
   113	  arXiv:1003.6007).
   114	- **Type $B_3$ positive monoid, standard generators:** Iqbal–Munir–Ayub–Nizami, Rev. Un. Mat.
   115	  Argentina 67(2) (2024) 503–516.
   116	- **All finite types, larger alphabets:** finite complete rewriting on all simple elements
   117	  (Hermiller–Meier, JPAA 136 (1999)); coherent convergent presentation on $W\setminus\{1\}$
   118	  (Gaussent–Guiraud–Malbos, arXiv:1203.5358, Prop. 3.2.1); finite quadratic convergent presentations
   119	  on finite Garside families for every finitely generated Artin–Tits monoid (Dehornoy–Guiraud,
   120	  arXiv:1504.02717).
   121	- **Regular normal forms:** lex-minimal positive braid words are regular in type $A$
   122	  (Flores–González-Meneses, arXiv:1808.02755); finite-state geodesic cross-sections on standard atoms
   123	  for all finite-type Artin monoids (Fuchiwaki–Fujii–Saito–Tsuchioka, RIMS 1646, 2008), not
   124	  lex-minimal. No source found giving a regular lex-minimal language on $\{\sigma_i,\Delta^{\pm1}\}$ for all
   125	  finite types.
   126	- **Coxeter groups (question 1):** finite types $A,B,D$ (Bokut–Shiao 2001), $E_6,E_7$ (D. Lee 2008),
   127	  $H_{2,3,4}$ (Lee–Lee, arXiv:1809.08419), $G_2,F_4,E_{6,7,8}$ (Pang–Wang, arXiv:2002.07369 v2, 2026);
   128	  Bokut–Shiao conjecture refuted (Chen–Liu, arXiv:0910.0096).
